Package: Pando
Version: 2.0.5
Type: Package
Title: Inferring regulomes from multi-modal single-cell genomics data
Authors@R: person(given = "Jonas Simon",
               family = "Fleck",
               role = c("aut", "cre"),
               email = "jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch",
               comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4686-7254"))
Maintainer: Jonas Simon Fleck <jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch>
Description: Pando jointly uses scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq measurements to infer
    regulatory relationships between TF-binding site pairs and target genes.
    For two or more conditions within a broad cell type, infer_condition_grn
    keeps the canonical two-stage common-dictionary procedure. Candidate edges
    are discovered on the complete cell type and separately in every condition
    using the original Pando peak-to-gene, motif, peak-target-correlation and
    TF-target-correlation steps, and exact TF-peak-target triples are unioned
    into one frozen dictionary. Instead of independent unregularized Gaussian
    GLMs, every target is then fitted jointly across conditions by multi-task
    ridge regression. TF-by-ATAC predictors use one pooled training reference
    for centering and scaling, while exported coefficients are back-transformed
    to the original TF-by-ATAC units for downstream projection. A positive
    ridge term makes the fitted system identifiable under collinearity or raw
    rank deficiency, and a symmetric fusion penalty shrinks condition
    coefficients toward one another without deleting dictionary edges. Each
    fitted condition receives equal total loss weight so large conditions do
    not dominate the joint coefficient solution. One target-specific lambda is
    selected for all conditions by condition-stratified cross-validation, using
    the one-standard-error rule by default. Raw design rank,
    condition-specific zero variance, regularized condition number and effective
    degrees of freedom remain available as diagnostics. The public
    target-condition rsq field uses out-of-fold R-squared, while in-sample
    R-squared is retained separately; raw rank deficiency no longer invalidates
    a target when the regularized fit succeeds. Approximate ridge-Wald standard
    errors and P values are retained for the existing BH coefficient contract,
    and only adjusted-P values below the configured threshold enter
    penalty_effect. When no condition column is supplied, the column is absent,
    or fewer than two levels are observed, the original per-cell-type infer_grn
    Gaussian interaction workflow is used. Independent cell-type jobs can be
    dispatched through BiocParallel without nested worker pools, and bundled
    reference datasets are installed as standalone RData files.
